"JH" <no@email> writes:
> I was looking around at the source, and it appears that it uses the PM_
> flags to find race, thus humans can't eat any monster with PM_HUMAN set.

You mean M2_HUMAN. PM_HUMAN refers to the human monster, which
generally only exists as corpses.

> However, for my draconian race, I'd want to make all types of dragons
> cannibalism.  How could I do this?  I suppose I could add a PM_DRAGON that
> is set for all current dragon types, but that seems a little extreme, is
> there a more obvious way I'm missing?

You could kludge your_race() along the lines of (not at all tested):

#define your_race(ptr)   ((((ptr)->mflags2 & urace.selfmask) != 0L) || \
                (urace.malenum == PM_DRACONIAN && (ptr)->mlet == S_DRAGON))

but adding a M2_DRAGON monster flag (0x00004000 would be the obvious
value to give it) for dragons-and-draconians and putting it in
draconians' selfmask would be much cleaner.

(While you were at it, you could change Dragonbane's S_DRAGON to
M2_DRAGON to make its special attack work against draconians as well;
you'd need to change its SPFX_DCLAS to SPFX_DFLAG2 to let the code
know you'd done that.)

